  "notes": [
    "**Enojarse** is the reflexive form of **enojar** (to anger/annoy)",
    "Regular **-AR verb** with reflexive pronouns",
    "No spelling changes or stem changes",
    "Used with \"con\" to indicate who you're angry with: *enojarse con alguien* (to get angry with someone)",
    "Non-reflexive **enojar**: to anger, to annoy (someone else)",
    "Common in Latin America; in Spain, **enfadarse** is more common",
    "Common usage: *Me enojé con mi hermano* (I got angry with my brother), *No te enojes* (Don't get angry)",
    "Related adjective: **enojado/a** (angry/mad)"
  ],
